cff-version: 1.2.0
title: BibNexus
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
abstract: >-
  BibNexus is a local-first desktop application for bibliographic data
  management and cleaning, purpose-built for the data-preparation stage of
  bibliometric analysis, systematic reviews and meta-analyses. It imports
  reference records exported from Web of Science, Scopus, PubMed, Embase,
  EndNote and major Chinese databases (CNKI, Wanfang, VIP, Yiigle), and
  standardizes author addresses, institution names, countries and cited
  references during import. Within a single workspace it provides isolated
  multi-library management, classification, reading screening, fast and
  advanced search, duplicate detection and removal, batch field editing, a
  recycle bin with undo/redo, and a local data-statistics workbench. Cleaned
  records can be exported as Web of Science tagged plain text or EndNote CIW to
  feed downstream tools such as CiteSpace, VOSviewer and Bibliometrix. BibNexus
  focuses on reliable local data curation and does not itself perform network
  visualization or knowledge-graph rendering.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lu
    given-names: Huan
    affiliation: "Ecoo Network Technology, Nanning, China"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4341-8773"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-06-23"
url: "https://www.bibnexus.com"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/bibnexus/BibNexus/releases"
keywords:
  - literature management
  - bibliometrics
  - reference deduplication
  - data cleaning
  - systematic review
